Capacity [text box] - PlaceBuffer
Type the Capacity into the text box, i.e., the number of places of the PlaceBuffer.
Remarks
Type in -1 for an unlimited number of places if Sequentially Indexing is active. You can access the
individual places of the PlaceBuffer by their index. You can only reduce the Capacity, if enough places are
empty.
You can only change the Capacity if no parts are located in the PlaceBuffer, i.e., if it is empty.
SimTalk
Capacity [SimTalk] - PlaceBuffer
See also
Sequentially Indexing [check box]
Capacity [text box] - PlaceBuffer
11-2046 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Sequentially Indexing [check box]
To only start the Processing Time on a place of the PlaceBuffer when the succeeding place is free, select
this check box.
Remarks
Note
In Sequentially Indexing mode, the Processing Time does not represent the time for which a part is
processed on a place, but the time used for moving the part from its current place to the succeeding
place. Suppose that we have a capacity of four, then the Processing Time passes three times before the
part can leave the PlaceBuffer, because three move processes have to take place.
The total time can get longer because of waiting times. For this reason no time is used on the last place
and the part can exit the PlaceBuffer immediately once it reaches the last place, provided the successor
can accept the part.
If Sequentially Indexing is cleared, the default behavior of the PlaceBuffer applies.
You can only set the Processing Time for the PlaceBuffer as a whole, not for the individual places.
The Processing Time is equally distributed across all places and divided by the number of places. For a
Processing Time of one minute and a capacity of three places each place has a processing time of 20
seconds.
SimTalk
SequentiallyIndexing [SimTalk]
See also
Processing Time [PlaceBuffer]
Capacity [text box] - PlaceBuffer
Sequentially Indexing [check box]
Plant Simulation Help 11-2047
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Accumulating [check box] - PlaceBuffer
To make the MUs accumulate on the PlaceBuffer, select this check box.
Remarks
Accumulating behavior enables the MUs to move front to end to each other, if the exit of the PlaceBuffer
is Blocked.
To make the MUs retain their distance to each other, i.e., to make all succeeding MUs stop moving when
the preceding part cannot exit the PlaceBuffer, clear Accumulating. If the preceding part cannot exit and if
Accumulating is cleared, no additional MU can enter the PlaceBuffer.
SimTalk
Accumulating [SimTalk] - PlaceBuffer
Tab Times
Tab Times [PlaceBuffer]
Define Times as described under the Tab Times.
Select a distribution from the drop-down list and type the values that this distribution requires into the
text box. Plant Simulation shows the parameters along the upper border of the tab. You can also select a
constant time (Const).
Note
You can only type in a constant Processing Time for the parts in the PlaceBuffer, no statistical
distributions, no dependencies from the part type or no formulas.
You can set the type of the distribution and a complete set of parameters with the method
setTypeAndAttr [SimTalk].
