Processing Time [PlaceBuffer]
Type in the Processing Time of MUs in the PlaceBuffer.
Remarks
You can only specify a constant Processing Time for the parts in the PlaceBuffer. You can neither select a
probability distribution, nor a dependency on the MU type, nor a formula.
For the PlaceBuffer the Processing Time is more of a Dwelling Time than a Processing Time as the parts
are not really being processed, but buffered and then moved on.
If Sequentially Indexing is cleared, you can only set the Processing Time for the PlaceBuffer as a whole,
not for the individual places. The Processing Time is equally distributed across all places. For a Processing
Time of one minute and a Capacity of three places each place has a processing time of 20 seconds.
If Sequentially Indexing is selected, the Processing Time for moving the part on to the next place is used
up. For a Capacity of four the threefold Processing Time passes at least before the part can leave the
PlaceBuffer, as three move processes have to take place. The time can be extended through waiting times.
